---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CtaSection from '../components/sections/CtaSection.astro';
import Icon from '../components/icons/Icon.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Chancey — A lottery toolkit for adults 18+"
  description="Chancey is a lottery toolkit for adults 18+ who already play. We do not sell tickets, predict numbers, or run ads inside the app."
  pageType="AboutPage"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
    { name: 'About', href: '/about/' },
  ]}
>
  <section class="container">
    <div class="article">
      <header>
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1>A lottery toolkit that handles the boring parts.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Chancey helps you pick lottery numbers and track the tickets you buy. That's the whole
          product. No sales pitch, no fake systems, no ads.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section>
        <h2>What Chancey is</h2>
        <p>
          Chancey is a lottery app for adults 18+. The number builder helps you pick and save sets
          of numbers. The tracker scans printed tickets and checks each one against the official
          draw results. It works in any modern web browser. iPhone and Android apps are on the
          way.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What Chancey is not</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Not a lottery retailer. We do not sell tickets or pay prizes.</li>
          <li>Not part of any state, provincial, or national lottery.</li>
          <li>Not a predictor. Lottery draws are random. The builder cannot beat the odds.</li>
          <li>Not an ad business. Ticket photos are never used to target ads.</li>
          <li>Not a tool to bring in new lottery players.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Principles</h2>
        <h3>The lottery is the source of truth</h3>
        <p>
          Chancey shows what it sees from the lottery's posted results. If Chancey and the lottery
          ever disagree, the lottery is right.
        </p>
        <h3>Honesty over hype</h3>
        <p>
          The number builder is for fun and organization. It does not improve the odds of any
          draw. We say so anywhere a feature could sound like a prediction.
        </p>
        <h3>Privacy by default</h3>
        <p>
          We collect only what we need to run the app. We do not sell ticket photos, browsing data,
          or contact info. The full <a href="/privacy/">Privacy policy</a> spells out what we keep
          and why.
        </p>
        <h3>No engagement traps</h3>
        <p>
          No streaks, no badges, no "we miss you" emails. The app is useful when you open it. It
          stays quiet when you don't.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Who this is for</h2>
        <p>
          Adults who already play the lottery — once a week or once in a while — and want their
          tickets out of the camera roll and into something they can search. Chancey is not built
          to recruit new lottery players. It also points you to help if play feels heavier than it
          should.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Where Chancey works</h2>
        <p>
          Today: any modern web browser at <a href={site.appUrl}>{site.appUrl}</a>. The site you're
          reading is the marketing front door at <a href={site.url}>{site.domain}</a>. iPhone and
          Android apps are on the roadmap.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Get in touch</h2>
        <p>
          Send us a message through the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>. A real person reads
          every message and replies within two business days. Pick the topic that matches what you
          need — general, support, privacy, feedback, bug, or security.
        </p>
        <div class="notice">
          <span class="notice-icon" aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="heart" size={22} /></span>
          <div>
            <strong>Need help with gambling?</strong>
            In the United States, call or text 1‑800‑GAMBLER for free, confidential support 24/7.
            Outside the U.S., look up your local problem-gambling helpline.
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaSection
    heading="Track your next ticket."
    description="The web app is free and works on any device. Pick a set, scan a ticket, and see what Chancey does."
  />
</BaseLayout>
